<title>HUNGARY: NOVOTRADE SWINGS TO OPER. PROFIT IN H1.</title>
<headline>NOVOTRADE SWINGS TO OPER. PROFIT IN H1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June 30.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				    Jan-June 1997	 Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>    Operating result	    89.6 profit   vs	65.5 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     182.8	    vs     168.1</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	   151.5	    vs     157.1</p>
<p>    Net sales		  3,418.5	    vs   1,834.3</p>
<p>     Domestic sales	  2,538.1	    vs   1,113.7</p>
<p>     Export sales		880.4	    vs     720.6</p>
<p>    Other revenues	     210.4	    vs     163.0</p>
<p>    Financial profit	    98.1	    vs	28.4</p>
<p>    Extraordinary revenues     2.6	    vs     297.2</p>
<p>    Extraord. expenditures     7.5	    vs	92.1</p>
<p>    Extraordinary result	 4.9 loss     vs     205.1 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is  Novotrade Rt. The figures are consolidated, unaudited, and were calculated according to the Hungarian Accounting Standards (HAS). Novotrade is a holding compani. It was 51.8 percent owned by Deutsche Kassenverein AG on June 30.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that its operating profit improved due to a stricter control on costs at the members of the group. The company's financial revenues rose by 70 million forint due to profits on the sale of stocks, Novotrade said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
